+## Sites
+
+A request names its site in the `X-Larder-Site` header (`main`, `annex`);
+without the header the site is `main`. An unknown site is a 400 with the
+code `unknown_site`, on every route.
+
+Batches, stock on hand (`onHand` in the item routes and
+`/export/stock.csv`), cooking, waste, alerts, `/reports/stock-value` and
+stock-takes only see the request's site: a batch, location or stock-take of
+another site answers as if it did not exist, and an order is received into
+the request's site. Items, suppliers, prices, orders, recipes and dishes are
+shared. The waste report, forecasts, temperature logs, the ledger export and
+the nightly job cover every site.
+
